package mc.fenix.charts;

import mc.fenix.charts.GemCandlestickChartTypes.GemCandlestickChartData;

/**
  A candlestick chart displays important datapoints for a (short) period of time,
  and is often used to show how stock prices changed over said periods. Each
  candlestick's horizontal position represents time, while its vertical bar and
  the line crossing through it represent the opening, closing, highest, and lowest
  price of that period. The candlestick's color indicates whether the price went
  up (green) or down (red), which determines whether the top of the bar shows the
  opening or closing price (and vice versa for the bottom).

  For example, it can be used to visualize the daily price movements of a stock
  or cryptocurrency over the course of a month.
*/
component GemCandlestickChart(
  /** The data entries to be displayed in the candlestick chart. Each entry is expected to provide values in the order: open, high, low, close. */
  GemCandlestickChartData data,
  /** Whether the chart's configuration panel is shown. */
  boolean showConfig = false
)
